# block_expr.tkr — §9 E Block-B in expression position (ruling 7), exercised end to end on the host
# build. A brace group in EXPRESSION position is a value-producing block whose TRAILING expression is
# its value, running INLINE in the enclosing frame. Each row addresses its case BY NAME: `main.tks`
# asserts the case's own value with `teko::assert::eq_i64` and announces `scenario <name>: ok`, which
# the row below demands. The same program runs through the native inline-block lowering and the C GNU
# statement-expression lowering; a divergence in either backend fails its row.

Feature: block_expr — a Block-B in expression position yields its trailing value, inline in the frame

  Scenario: block_value_trailing_expr — a Block-B's value is its trailing expression
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "scenario block_value_trailing_expr: ok"

  Scenario: block_nested_value — a Block-B nests inside another Block-B
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "scenario block_nested_value: ok"

  Scenario: block_runs_inline_in_frame — a Block-B reads and writes an enclosing var, inline
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "scenario block_runs_inline_in_frame: ok"

  Scenario: block_as_call_argument — a Block-B stands in argument position
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "scenario block_as_call_argument: ok"

  Scenario: block_and_construction_coexist — a Block-B and a §9 B construction coexist unambiguously
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "scenario block_and_construction_coexist: ok"

  Scenario: closure_body_block_anchor — a closure body is itself a Block-B (spine anchor)
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "scenario closure_body_block_anchor: ok"

  Scenario: capture_by_copy_snapshot — a closure captures its free variable by copy (spine anchor)
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "scenario capture_by_copy_snapshot: ok"
